provenance.prompt:
Create an original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96. Use the supplied Leo gameplay sprite only as an identity and pixel-art style reference. Draw exactly five distinct complete full-body Leo poses in a strict three-column by two-row grid, row-major; leave the sixth cell fully transparent. Broad transparent gutters; full hair, hands and shoes inside each pose cell. Same scale and camera. Crisp readable 1990s arcade pixel-art clusters and dark outlines.

Leo is the pale aristocratic adult human captain of the Blackthorn Court Kings. Preserve pale skin, long wavy black hair, refined mustache, composed face, natural adult anatomy and patient poise. He wears a tailored black basketball uniform with restrained crimson accents, matching shorts and shoes. Exactly two arms, two hands, two legs and two shoes. No fangs, horns, cape, robe, monster traits, extra limbs, costume changes or props.

This is a right-facing rebound. The basketball is separate game art. Leo’s hands remain empty in every drawing; no ball is present even at the catch point. Do not draw any sphere, orb, seams, court, hoop, floor, ground shadow, background, glow, border, grid, text, teammate or opponent. Exterior and gutters are true alpha-zero transparency, no checkerboard, matte, speckles or haze.

Five distinct connected poses:
0 sets his feet under the falling ball, eyes up, knees flexed and hands ready;
1 jumps vertically, both arms reach high and slightly toward image-right;
2 reaches at the apex, fingers spread to tip/grab the separate ball, face focused;
3 GRAB at simulation tick5: hands close around empty air at the catch point, elbows start drawing down;
4 lands under control in a composed ready stance, hands empty after securing the separate ball.

Keep Leo pale, human, long-haired, mustached and recognizable in the black/crimson Court Kings uniform. Preserve complete anatomy and natural joints. Return only the transparent sprite sheet.
